title: VMware Aria Automation: Node
agents: aria_automation
catalog: app/vmware
license: GPLv2
distribution: kuhn-ruess
description:
 The special agent queries '/api/v1/services/cluster' on an Aria Automation
 node. Every node answers with all services of the cluster and the instances
 on all nodes. The agent finds the queried node in this data by its node name
 (host name by default, compared case insensitive, in full or by the first
 label) and only keeps the service instances of that node for this host.

 This service shows which node of the cluster data belongs to the host and
 how many service instances run on it. It is {CRIT} if the node name is not
 found in the cluster data; the details list the node names reported by the
 cluster, so the node name can be set in the special agent rule.

discovery:
 One service per host with the special agent.
